<title>FRANCE: Strafor buys French, German firms.</title>
<headline>Strafor buys French, German firms.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strafor-Facom said on Wednesday it has bought Beissbarth, a German garage equipment firm and Mecanobloc, a French specialist in partitions.</p>
<p>Facom, a wholly-owned Stafor Facom unit, bought Beissbarth, which has annual turnover of 340 million francs.</p>
<p>Mecanobloc, bought by another wholly-owned subsidiary, Clestra, has annual sales of 200 million francs.</p>
<p>Strafor Facom said the acquisitions were part of its strategy of focusing on office systems as well as hand tools and garage products.</p>
</text>
